# shell: desktop
# PVL-045: what the frames painted has to BE the window, not most of it.
# A window keeps its own pixels now, so a frame that skips a row leaves
# whatever was there -- and a check that looks at the pixels it thought to
# name would not notice the rest going stale.  This runs the things that
# change a listing and then holds the whole window against the picture a
# full redraw draws.
wait 8
note a selection, then another one: the row that lost it must lose it on
note screen too, and nobody damages a row for being deselected
click-row 1
wait 8
click-row 2
wait 8
expect-same-as-redraw
note a file arrives, a file goes, and a file changes under the window
write /tmp/trk_script/0a.txt x
wait 40
remove /tmp/trk_script/b.txt
wait 40
write /tmp/trk_script/a.txt hello there
wait 40
expect-same-as-redraw
note a band swept over the rows and let go, which leaves nothing behind
press 100 250
move 300 200
release 300 200
wait 20
expect-same-as-redraw
note and a drag that ends in a refusal: the alert is on the screen, and
note the picture the pointer was carrying is not
press-row 0
move-row 3
release-row 3
wait 20
expect-alert exists
expect-same-as-redraw
note and a rename box opened over a row, then abandoned
click-row 1
wait 8
key e ctrl
wait 20
key Escape
wait 20
expect-same-as-redraw
quit
